  m_Name: Journal_caches
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  id: journal.caches
  title: "Not Every Signal Is History"
  author: "Prospector K. Oyelaran"
  dateLine: "Field note, near a cache"
  category: 2
  body: "A VALUABLE SIGNATURE on the scanner is a cache, not an archaeological site. Caches are shallow, buried less than a metre down, and once revealed they're marked with a gold border. You can dig them with the shovel without guilt.\n\nWhat you'll pull out is mostly minerals: copper, meteoric iron, the odd silver nugget or geode. Once in a while you'll find something rarer. Caches make useful money, but they're not part of the record, so don't confuse them with the real work."
  placement: 5
  bodyId: 
  siteIndex: 0
  order: 40
